<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>Air Hockey Table</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.8">model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
    <name>Cymbergaj</name>
    <email>azmozgame@gmail.com</email>
  </author>

  <description>
    Static air hockey table: countertop (play area) + cushion band, meshes
    exported from CAD (meters, Z-up). AprilTag 16h5 markers are placed as
    flat decals at the positions measured in table_markers.yml, converted
    from the perception code's table-frame (mm, origin at one play-area
    corner) into this model's CAD frame (origin at the opposite corner).

    band.obj is a locally patched copy of table_models/band.obj: the
    original CAD export had the cushion's tall skirt hanging below the
    play surface instead of standing above it (visually "upside down").
    It's mirrored here about the z=0.01 flush plane (with face winding
    reversed to keep normals/collision outward-facing) so the wall now
    rises ~55mm above the play surface. Fix the source export in
    Inventor and re-copy when convenient - this patch only lives in this
    package's meshes/ copy, not in table_models/.
  </description>
</model>
